    92	
    93	### 5. Project memory check
    94	
    95	Check `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/` for the project memory baseline:
    96	
    97	- If `README.md` is missing OR `design/` is empty OR `features/` is empty → project memory is sparse. Run AskUserQuestion: "Project memory looks thin. Run the interview skill to populate it before starting work?" If the user accepts, load the [`interview` skill](../interview/SKILL.md) and run the 5-wave bootstrap; the workflow resumes after the interview completes.
    98	- If project memory is populated → proceed directly to the workflow.
    99	
   100	### 6. Enter the workflow
   101	
   102	Hand off to the `orchestration` skill's state machine. The first productive step is **Ideation** — load the [`ideation` skill](../ideation/SKILL.md) and follow its DISCUSSION → WORK → EVALUATION → MEMORIZATION procedure. The orchestration skill steers transitions between the six steps.
   103	
   104	---
   105	
   106	## Glossary
   107	
   108	Gobbi-specific terms used throughout the skill tree. Load this section to anchor vocabulary before reading procedures.
   109	
   110	| Term | Definition |
   111	|---|---|
   112	| **Phase** | One of the 6 workflow steps: Configuration / Ideation / Preparation / Planning / Execution / Wrap-up. Each productive phase (all but Configuration) runs as a Loop. |
   113	| **Loop** | A workflow step's 4-sub-phase iteration: DISCUSSION → WORK → EVALUATION → MEMORIZATION. Every productive phase is structured as a loop body. |
   114	| **Sub-phase** | One of the 4 phases inside a loop: DISCUSSION / WORK / EVALUATION / MEMORIZATION. |
   115	| **Iter** | One iteration through a loop (iter1, iter2, …). Evaluation findings trigger a new iter when verdict is REVISE. |
   116	| **Verdict** | PASS / REVISE / FAIL — the evaluation outcome emitted at the end of a loop's EVALUATION sub-phase. |
   117	| **Disposition** | Finding lifecycle state: open / addressed / disputed / deferred / superseded. Used in evaluation artifacts and mistake entries. |
   118	| **Staging** | Session-scoped write path (`sessions/{date}-{session-id}/{loop}/staging/`) for findings, decisions, and mistake-candidates awaiting Wrap-up promotion. Agents write here; Wrap-up is the sole writer to project memory. |
   119	| **Sole-writer** | Wrap-up's MEMORIZATION is the only agent permitted to write finalized artifacts to project memory (`.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/...`). Interview is the documented bootstrap exception. |
   120	
   121	---
   122	
   123	## Workflow Overview
   124	
   125	The 6-step state machine and who owns each step:
   126	
   127	| Step | Phase | Owner | Specialist agents spawned | Purpose |
   128	|---|---|---|---|---|
   129	| **Configuration** | session init | manager + user | — | Session start, settings, project memory check, workflow configuration |
   130	| **Ideation** | Loop body | manager + user + leader | leader (DISCUSSION) | Refine What / Why / How until the idea is concrete enough to plan against |
   131	| **Preparation** | Loop body | manager + user + leader | leader (DISCUSSION) | Verify readiness — project memory + workspace skills against the locked Ideation output; close gaps |
   132	| **Planning** | Loop body | manager + user + leader | leader (DISCUSSION) | Decompose into ordered tasks with agent assignments + verification anchors |
   133	| **Execution** | Loop body, per-task | manager + user + executor | executor (WORK, one per task) | Implement each task within scope, with fresh verification evidence |
   134	| **Wrap-up** | Loop body | manager + user + assistant | assistant (WORK) | Promote session staging → project memory; write the handoff; emit `workflow.finish` |

